253
00:09:44,051 --> 00:09:46,153
and I don't know
all the drivers.

254
00:09:46,186 --> 00:09:48,288
-How about these trucks
that are in here now?

255
00:09:48,321 --> 00:09:50,323
-Well, this one and this one

256
00:09:50,357 --> 00:09:52,159
are a couple of my regular
customers.

257
00:09:52,192 --> 00:09:53,894
That one's a cross-country job

258
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,963
that came in last night
for an ignition check.

259
00:09:55,996 --> 00:09:57,898
I didn't see who the driver was.

260
00:09:57,931 --> 00:09:59,166
The nightman took care of it.

261
00:09:59,199 --> 00:10:00,834
-Okay if I look it over?
-Sure, go ahead.

262
00:10:00,868 --> 00:10:02,169
-This little honey?

263
00:10:02,202 --> 00:10:03,671
Oh, yeah, it's a smart
little number.

264
00:10:03,704 --> 00:10:06,606
I can see you're a man
who knows his trucks.

265
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,341
This one's got all the candy.

266
00:10:08,375 --> 00:10:10,110
Going after Moon men,
this is perfect.

267
00:10:10,143 --> 00:10:12,012
It's a real honey.

268
00:10:12,045 --> 00:10:13,613
Yep, real crates and everything.

269
00:10:13,647 --> 00:10:17,184
**

270
00:10:17,217 --> 00:10:18,786
Hi.
-Get away from that truck.

271
00:10:18,819 --> 00:10:20,253
-Hey. What's going on?

272
00:10:20,287 --> 00:10:21,655
-Frisk him.

273
00:10:21,689 --> 00:10:22,956
Stay out of this
or you'll get hurt.

274
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,391
-Now, look. I don't want
any trouble in here.

275
00:10:24,424 --> 00:10:26,526
-So I'm just gonna hit you
with this crowbar.

276
00:10:28,595 --> 00:10:31,899
-Hey, Joel. Do mechanics fight
better than scientists do?

277
00:10:31,932 --> 00:10:34,101
-Well, they often have heavy
wrenches in their hand,

278
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:35,568
so they do a lot better.
-Oh.

279
00:10:35,602 --> 00:10:39,272
**

280
00:10:39,306 --> 00:10:43,176
-Nobody touches
my Snap-on tools.

281
00:10:43,210 --> 00:10:44,344
Cool.

282
00:10:44,377 --> 00:10:45,512
-Hey.
-Just a little thing I made.

283
00:10:45,545 --> 00:10:47,114
I knew we'd use them sometime.

284
00:10:49,382 --> 00:10:51,318
-Cool.

285
00:10:51,351 --> 00:10:54,121
-Pretty neat, huh?

286
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:56,289
-Hey, that guy
wrenched his back.

287
00:10:56,323 --> 00:10:57,991
-He really socketed that guy.

288
00:10:58,025 --> 00:10:59,059
-[Laughs]

289
00:10:59,092 --> 00:11:01,261
He's hammered!

290
00:11:01,294 --> 00:11:03,596
**

291
00:11:03,630 --> 00:11:07,334
[Clattering]

292
00:11:07,367 --> 00:11:09,870
-Do, ooh, ooh.

293
00:11:11,438 --> 00:11:12,639
Ooh, he bench-pressed him.

294
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:14,241
[Chuckles]

295
00:11:14,274 --> 00:11:18,979
**

296
00:11:19,012 --> 00:11:20,280
-Ooh.

297
00:11:20,313 --> 00:11:22,182
-Oh, look.
He's getting tired.

298
00:11:22,215 --> 00:11:25,919
-What a retread.

299
00:11:25,953 --> 00:11:27,120
-It's the vice squad.

300
00:11:27,154 --> 00:11:29,322
-It's John Cleese, you bastard.

301
00:11:29,356 --> 00:11:30,991
-Let's roll.

302
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:36,463
**

303
00:11:36,496 --> 00:11:41,902
**

304
00:11:41,935 --> 00:11:44,738
-Well, at least he's getting
used to being beat up.

305
00:11:44,772 --> 00:11:47,674
-Hey, he's not even hurt.

306
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:50,310
They must have been using
Nerf tools or something.

307
00:11:50,343 --> 00:11:52,679
[Engine revs]

308
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:54,481
Not even a scratch.

309
00:11:58,518 --> 00:12:00,287
-* Underoos are fun to wear

310
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:01,789
-The truckload of radios
was a phony.

311
00:12:01,822 --> 00:12:03,223
-* And I can fly from
here to there *

312
00:12:03,256 --> 00:12:04,457
-The whole back end
was a fake door,

313
00:12:04,491 --> 00:12:07,160
and I'm sure they're planning on
hiding something inside.

314
00:12:07,194 --> 00:12:10,230
-Probably a ray gun.
-That's what I'm afraid of.

315
00:12:10,263 --> 00:12:12,766
They'll probably start blasting
again any time now.

316
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:14,301
I've sent Ted out to the airport

317
00:12:14,334 --> 00:12:16,136
to stand by on a plane
with some light bombs.

318
00:12:16,169 --> 00:12:18,471
-He hasn't been able to lift
heavy bombs since his hernia.

319
00:12:18,505 --> 00:12:20,273
-I'll fly out
and try to locate that truck,

320
00:12:20,307 --> 00:12:22,009
then radio Ted to bomb it.

321
00:12:22,042 --> 00:12:24,411
[Telephone rings]

322
00:12:24,444 --> 00:12:26,346
Cody Laboratory.
-Uh, Mr. Cody.

323
00:12:26,379 --> 00:12:28,115
I'm so upset.
They just blasted a troop train

324
00:12:28,148 --> 00:12:29,516
on the east end
of Carson Valley.

325
00:12:29,549 --> 00:12:31,151
I'm here all by myself,
and I don't what to do.

326
00:12:31,184 --> 00:12:32,352
Please help.
-They just blasted a troop

327
00:12:32,385 --> 00:12:33,921
train on the east end
of Carson Valley.

328
00:12:33,954 --> 00:12:35,322
Radio Ted to take off
on a plane...

329
00:12:35,355 --> 00:12:36,456
-Uncanny.
-...and watch them fly around

330
00:12:36,489 --> 00:12:37,657
out there. I'll contact him

331
00:12:37,690 --> 00:12:38,926
as soon as I spot the truck.

332
00:12:38,959 --> 00:12:41,628
-Right away.

333
00:12:41,661 --> 00:12:44,731
-Hello, Domino's.
-Calling Ted Richards.

334
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:46,299
Calling Ted Richards.

335
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:53,606
-Nipple, nipple, tweak,
tweak, fly!

336
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,843
-Whoa!

337
00:12:55,876 --> 00:12:59,813
**

338
00:12:59,847 --> 00:13:01,414
-Phew!

339
00:13:01,448 --> 00:13:03,583
**

340
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,418
Boy, he's got a nasty tailwind.

341
00:13:05,452 --> 00:13:07,320
-Must have been
something he ate.

342
00:13:07,354 --> 00:13:09,990
-Shouldn't they take off
before they crop dust?

343
00:13:10,023 --> 00:13:12,159
Unless we're doing ginseng.
-Yeah, ginseng.

344
00:13:15,863 --> 00:13:17,297
-Fly the plane, Ted.

345
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:18,565
Get the girl, Ted.

346
00:13:18,598 --> 00:13:21,101
Oh, I'm gonna
show him something.

347
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:27,507
**

348
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:34,247
**

349
00:13:34,281 --> 00:13:35,715
-Calling Ted Richards.

350
00:13:37,985 --> 00:13:39,953
Calling Ted Richards.

351
00:13:39,987 --> 00:13:41,088
-Who is it?
-This is Ted. Come in.

352
00:13:41,121 --> 00:13:42,923
-Who do you think, dolt?
-I spot the truck.

353
00:13:42,956 --> 00:13:44,124
It's going a long a dirt road

354
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:46,059
just east of the end
of the valley.

355
00:13:46,093 --> 00:13:47,995
-I'll be right with you.
-Okay.

356
00:13:48,028 --> 00:13:50,463
I'll keep them in sight
until you show up.

357
00:13:50,497 --> 00:13:53,600
-Does Cody normally travel
with a full radio pack on?

358
00:13:57,938 --> 00:13:59,372
-It's his radio flyer.

359
00:14:02,142 --> 00:14:03,543
-Flying ham outfit.

360
00:14:05,879 --> 00:14:07,414
-Hey, UPS.

361
00:14:07,447 --> 00:14:11,251
Cody must be tracing a package
or something.

362
00:14:11,284 --> 00:14:13,720
-Now this is the third time
I've done

363
00:14:13,753 --> 00:14:16,924
this "Camouflaged Destruction"
scene, so listen up.

364
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:22,095
-Cody's after us again!
-We'll stop him.

365
00:14:22,129 --> 00:14:24,597
Use the rifle.

366
00:14:24,631 --> 00:14:26,033
-That should stop him.

367
00:14:29,536 --> 00:14:31,071
Pull.

368
00:14:31,104 --> 00:14:32,973
[Gunshot]

369
00:14:33,006 --> 00:14:34,107
-Whoa.
-Look out.

370
00:14:34,141 --> 00:14:35,308
-Missed him. Drift left.

371
00:14:35,342 --> 00:14:37,277
Pull.

372
00:14:37,310 --> 00:14:38,511
[Gunshot]

373
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:41,949
**

374
00:14:41,982 --> 00:14:44,651
-Oh, they got homicide doors
on that thing.

375
00:14:44,684 --> 00:14:47,554
-Did you get him?
-No, but I scared him off.

376
00:14:47,587 --> 00:14:50,390
-So he can fly back and tell
the cops where we are?

377
00:14:50,423 --> 00:14:53,426
-So what? By the time they get
out here, we'll be long gone.

378
00:14:53,460 --> 00:14:58,765
**

379
00:14:58,798 --> 00:15:04,171
**

380
00:15:04,204 --> 00:15:06,839
-Ted, Ted.
-This is Ted.

381
00:15:06,873 --> 00:15:08,308
-Who is it?
-It's me.

382
00:15:08,341 --> 00:15:09,842
It's always going to be me.

383
00:15:09,876 --> 00:15:11,778
Whoever calls you, it's me.

384
00:15:11,811 --> 00:15:13,280
-Right!
-Oh.

385
00:15:13,313 --> 00:15:21,454
**

386
00:15:21,488 --> 00:15:29,963
**

387
00:15:29,997 --> 00:15:38,671
**

388
00:15:38,705 --> 00:15:40,307
-Let me get that door for you.

389
00:15:42,609 --> 00:15:44,277
Yeah.

390
00:15:44,311 --> 00:15:47,180
**

391
00:15:47,214 --> 00:15:49,082
-Yeah, just put that stuff
in the back.

392
00:15:49,116 --> 00:15:50,617
I kind of live
in my plane really.

393
00:15:50,650 --> 00:15:52,352
You know, if you want to put
the seat back, go ahead.

394
00:15:52,385 --> 00:15:56,089
You know, just make
yourself comfortable.

395
00:15:56,123 --> 00:15:57,890
-What gives?
-The truck's just ahead.

396
00:15:57,924 --> 00:15:59,792
Fly over that dirt road.

397
00:15:59,826 --> 00:16:01,494
-Okay.
-Where are the bombs?

398
00:16:01,528 --> 00:16:02,395
-Right there.

399
00:16:02,429 --> 00:16:09,769
**

400
00:16:09,802 --> 00:16:12,772
-Oh, could you guys have found
a smaller bomb?

401
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:15,642
What are the odds of a moving
plane hitting a moving target

402
00:16:15,675 --> 00:16:18,278
with a moving bomb
that looks like a pineapple?

403
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:20,180
Geez.
-Oh, great, double-oh Cody.

404
00:16:20,213 --> 00:16:22,615
Do you have a license
to kill now, Mr. Cody?

405
00:16:25,685 --> 00:16:27,154
-What was that?

406
00:16:27,187 --> 00:16:29,956
-Oh, just an exploding
dip in the road.

407
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,591
-There's a plane up there.
He must have bombed us.

408
00:16:31,624 --> 00:16:33,393
And it looks like he's coming
back for another try.

409
00:16:33,426 --> 00:16:34,627
-Uh-oh.

410
00:16:34,661 --> 00:16:37,064
-We'll give a blast
with our ray gun.

411
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:38,465
-That was pretty close,

412
00:16:38,498 --> 00:16:40,133
but drop down a little lower
next time.

413
00:16:40,167 --> 00:16:41,501
-This time, use a water
balloon.

414
00:16:41,534 --> 00:16:43,103
That'll really scare 'em.

415
00:16:43,136 --> 00:16:46,673
**

416
00:16:46,706 --> 00:16:48,808
-Hold it up right there.

417
00:16:48,841 --> 00:16:51,644
Let it out.

418
00:16:51,678 --> 00:16:53,280
-Okay. Let's see.

419
00:16:53,313 --> 00:16:55,482
Bathroom stuff, books,
nicknacks, kids' room.

420
00:16:55,515 --> 00:16:58,485
Hey, where's that
ray gun anyway?

421
00:16:58,518 --> 00:16:59,619
Oh!

422
00:16:59,652 --> 00:17:06,493
**

423
00:17:06,526 --> 00:17:08,595
-Hey, they've stopped!

424
00:17:08,628 --> 00:17:10,397
-Looks like they're aiming
a gun at us.

425
00:17:10,430 --> 00:17:12,899
Dive on them quick!
-But stay in the plane, Ted.

426
00:17:12,932 --> 00:17:17,137
**

427
00:17:17,170 --> 00:17:19,972
-Hurry it up!
He's diving on us again!

428
00:17:20,006 --> 00:17:23,676
-A blast from the Chevy horn.

429
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:25,745
-You missed!

430
00:17:25,778 --> 00:17:27,480
-Aimed too quick.
Turn the truck around.

431
00:17:27,514 --> 00:17:29,449
I'll get another shot at him.
-Right!

432
00:17:29,482 --> 00:17:39,426
**

433
00:17:39,459 --> 00:17:42,061
-Well, they missed,
but how are we gonna get

434
00:17:42,095 --> 00:17:44,464
a cliff-hanging ending
for this episode?

435
00:17:44,497 --> 00:17:47,066
-You know, my flying helmet's
really hard on my scalp, Ted.

436
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:48,501
How do you keep yours so smooth

437
00:17:48,535 --> 00:17:51,171
and young-looking besides
using shellac all the time?

438
00:17:51,204 --> 00:17:57,944
**

439
00:17:57,977 --> 00:18:04,817
**

440
00:18:04,851 --> 00:18:06,085
-Well, that's the end.

441
00:18:06,119 --> 00:18:07,454
Next week,
a new character for sure.

442
00:18:07,487 --> 00:18:08,555
There's no way you could
get a guy out of that one.

443
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:10,157
-Uh-uh.

444
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:16,963
**

445
00:18:16,996 --> 00:18:23,803
**

446
00:18:23,836 --> 00:18:30,643
**

